 flashrom_powerd.lock path  This updates the directory for flashrom_powerd.lock to use &quot;/run/lock&quot; instead of &quot;/var/lock&quot; as per FHS 3.0.  BUG=chromium:616620 CQ-DEPEND=CL:351271 BRANCH=none TEST=compiled  Change-Id: I26ece6b26f8cafa70d9fd0fe1a5047cc4a6299df Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351360 Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="351360" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/60/351360/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I12589e55fbe4eee5458727766065c3d3f479ff28" commit="16442d01c1074438c4a5c24abddbbfeae686d886" commit_message="site_tests: update lockfile path for flashrom  BUG=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:351360 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I12589e55fbe4eee5458727766065c3d3f479ff28 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/351318 Commit-Ready: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="351318" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/18/351318/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ia5fd6ccfd102b9a6cafa525f44c5da96b189efb5" commit="fe5f91d6dd7de8359f169721b07b96f9fd5abc2c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: tpm_tis: further simplify calculation of ordinal duration  commit 07b133e6060b (&quot;char/tpm: simplify duration calculation and eliminate smatch warning.&quot;) includes a misleading test that is always false. The tpm_ordinal_duration table is only valid for TPM_PROTECTED ordinals where the higher 16 bits are all 0, anyway.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54590 TEST=Build and boot on kevin, verify that /dev/tpm0 is present.  Signed-off-by: Martin Wilck &lt;Martin.Wilck@ts.fujitsu.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Peter Huewe &lt;peterhuewe@gmx.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit f728643001397cee39dcfabff6458a5fbc3baecf) Signed-off-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ia5fd6ccfd102b9a6cafa525f44c5da96b189efb5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354722 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354722" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/22/354722/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ib62b31dd65c8bc625445ee559f7abcbf9dd09460" commit="5393061c3541203fe95ee3128d475468afd6486d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: tpm_tis: Use devm_free_irq not free_irq  The interrupt is always allocated with devm_request_irq so it must always be freed with devm_free_irq.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54590 TEST=Build and boot on kevin, verify that /dev/tpm0 is present.  Fixes: 448e9c55c12d (&quot;tpm_tis: verify interrupt during init&quot;) Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe &lt;jgunthorpe@obsidianresearch.com&gt; Acked-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Martin Wilck &lt;Martin.Wilck@ts.fujitsu.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Peter Huewe &lt;peterhuewe@gmx.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 727f28b8ca24a581c7bd868326b8cea1058c720a) Signed-off-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: Ib62b31dd65c8bc625445ee559f7abcbf9dd09460 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354723 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354723" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/354723/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0cef5516cc70a07ffa88084d6b77637e0d1aeb35" commit="ef48ae68b79fdcf15348159d8cececd193909a7c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: tpm_tis: Ensure interrupts are disabled when the driver starts  This should be done very early, before anything could possibly cause the TPM to generate an interrupt. If the IRQ line is shared with another driver causing an interrupt before setting up our handler will be very bad.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54590 TEST=Build and boot on kevin, verify that /dev/tpm0 is present.  Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe &lt;jgunthorpe@obsidianresearch.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Martin Wilck &lt;Martin.Wilck@ts.fujitsu.com&gt; Tested-by: Scot Doyle &lt;lkml14@scotdoyle.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jarkko Sakkinen &lt;jarkko.sakkinen@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Peter Huewe &lt;peterhuewe@gmx.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 036bb38ffb3e4c92361108f324364b0341cd9e31) Signed-off-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I0cef5516cc70a07ffa88084d6b77637e0d1aeb35 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354724 Commit-Ready: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354724" owner_email="apronin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/24/354724/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie23f8a7f19baa874353416c4309a7859d55e8109" commit="96581da5a96184483c5f110416d910c827f74e92" commit_message="metrics: Add VeyronEmmcUpgrade CrOSEvent strings  This patch adds some event type strings to the CrOSEvent histogram that will be used to monitor the success of a one-time eMMC upgrade performed on Veyron devices.  BUG=chromium:599960 TEST=Ran 'metrics_client -v VeyronEmmcUpgrade.Success', saw no errors and a CrOSEvent entry show up in /var/lib/metrics/uma-events.  Change-Id: Ie23f8a7f19baa874353416c4309a7859d55e8109 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342782 Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342782" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/82/342782/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Idf4ff41b316533af69070bbd8b0b093fffe8de3a" commit="442b2331f31c5b1ae12827fa969bb99516714b50" commit_message="UPSTREAM: netfilter: Set /proc/net entries owner to root in namespace  Various files are owned by root with 0440 permission. Reading them is impossible in an unprivileged user namespace, interfering with firewall tools. For instance, iptables-save relies on /proc/net/ip_tables_names contents to dump only loaded tables.  This patch